# MDC Rule: WordPress/PHP Testing Best Practices

- Write unit tests for all critical business logic using PHPUnit (preferred) or Pest (if compatible with WordPress).
- Use integration tests for plugin/theme interactions with WordPress core.
- Mock external dependencies in tests.
- Ensure tests are isolated and repeatable.
- Run tests automatically in CI/CD pipelines.
- Maintain high test coverage and review coverage reports regularly.
- Ensure all tests are compatible with the current WordPress version.

This rule applies to all *.php files in all subdirectories.

// Example: PHPUnit test
class SampleTest extends WP_UnitTestCase {
    public function test_addition() {
        $this->assertEquals( 2, 1 + 1 );
    }
}

// Example: Pest test (if compatible)
test('addition works', function () {
    expect(1 + 1)->toBe(2);
});

